    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:12px;">
      <h2>How I actually work</h2>
      <p>It's one system, handled start to finish. You stay on the tools. I keep the phone ringing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dsteps">
      <div class="dstep">
        <div class="dstep-n">01</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Hyper-local ads</h3>
          <p>Facebook ads aimed at homeowners in the exact postcodes you cover. You set the budget, I build and run the campaigns.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dstep">
        <div class="dstep-n">02</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Real footage of your work</h3>
          <p>We come to you and film your real jobs, or work from footage of jobs you've already done. No stock, ever. Real work on camera is what stops the scroll.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dstep">
        <div class="dstep-n">03</div>
        <div>
          <h3>A qualifying funnel</h3>
          <p>The ad runs to a hand-coded page that filters out tyre-kickers, so only serious enquiries with a name, number, postcode and job type get through.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="dstep">
        <div class="dstep-n">04</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Leads to your phone</h3>
          <p>Verified leads land straight in your messages with automated follow-up behind them, so nothing goes cold while you're working. You quote, you win the job.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What I believe about trades marketing</h2>
      <p>A few things I won't budge on, because they're the whole point:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Real beats polished.</strong> A homeowner trusts real footage of a real job over a slick stock advert every time. So that's what we use.</li>
        <li><strong>A lead you can't tell apart from a time-waster is worthless.</strong> The funnel exists to filter, not just collect. Fewer, better enquiries beat a pile of cold form-fills.</li>
        <li><strong>No lock-in.</strong> No retainers, no long contracts. If it stops working, you stop. I'd rather earn your business month to month than tie you in.</li>
        <li><strong>You should always know where your money goes.</strong> Your ad spend goes direct to Facebook, never through me, and my fee is separate. No mystery.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where I work</h2>
      <p>I'm based in Edinburgh and work with trades across Scotland. A lot of my campaigns run around Edinburgh, Glasgow, Renfrewshire, Lanarkshire and West Lothian, but the targeting is built around your service area, not mine. If you get your work from homeowners in Scotland, you're covered.</p>
